"text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn9le05ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong italic\">Tanya and James text ...</span><br/><br/><span class=\"strong\"> Tanya</span>:  A strange young woman came into the coffee shop. She looks like she's been through a war!  Her hair is a mess and her jeans are torn. She has been sitting near me for a few minutes now drinking coffee. She's just been staring into space.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn9le05ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\"> James</span>:  Has she been mugged? Is she in shock? Has anyone called the police? What have the other people in the cafe been doing?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\"> Tanya</span>:  Everyone here has been ignoring her - like it's normal. She's covered in mud. How could that have happened? It hasn't been raining. The streets are dry!<br/><span class=\"strong\"> James</span>:   Have you tried to talk to her? If she hasn't been calling anyone herself maybe she's lost her phone!\n<br/><span class=\"strong\"> Tanya</span>:  Going over there now ... lol\n<br/><span class=\"strong\"> James</span>:  ???", "id": 2, "time": "13500", "image": "engenn9le05ob06re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Tanya</span>:  You won't believe it! I said I didn't mean to be nosy, but she looked like she's had a really bad day. Did she need help? She looked up at me and laughed. I recognized her immediately and felt so stupid!!! It was Nadia Travenski!\n<br/><span class=\"strong\"> James</span>:  NO WAY!<br/><span class=\"strong\"> Tanya</span>:  They're shooting an action movie in the building next door. She thought she would just hide out in here for a little break. She thanked me for my concern. When she finished, she paid her bill and mine.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\"> James</span>:  Did you get her autograph?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Tanya</span> : She's just come in again with the director ...  going to be an extra in the next scene!!!! Later ...", "id": 3, "time": "40500", "image": "engenn9le05ob06re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn9le05ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le05ob06re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Stories", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "What Happened to Her?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Relate information about problems.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect vs. Past Simple ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>:<br></li><li>For something that began in the past and continues into the present time. </li></ul> Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> I have learned a lot in this class.</span> <br><br> </li><li>For something that has been done several times. </li></ul>Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">She has called her mom many times. </span> <br> <br></li><li>For experiences up to the present. </li></ul> Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">This is the worst day we've ever had.</span> <br><br></li><li> For something that happened in the past but is relevant at the time of speaking. </li></ul>  Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> I can't call her. I've lost my cellphone. </span> <br> <br> </li><li>For referring to a time that is not yet finished. </li></ul> Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Have you played the guitar this week?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past</span>: <br></li><li>  For something that finished at a specific time in the past. </li></ul>  Example: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">I wrote that letter two weeks ago. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you can answer the question 'When?', the past time is stated or inferred or understood. Use the Past Simple. There is no connection to the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you cannot answer the question 'When?', because the time is not stated or not important, then choose the Present Perfect tense. There is instead a connection to the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sentence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">When she finished, she paid her bill and mine.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when she finished (her coffee)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> She's just come in again with the director ... </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  from the time she left  to now\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "A strange young woman came into the coffee shop. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She looks like she's been through a war!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I didn't mean to be nosy, but she looked like she's had a really bad day. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Did she need help? ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense </span> to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about experiences. When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span>, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. <br> To put emphasis on the result of the action, use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>.<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Has anyone called the police?</span></li></ul> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous tense </span> to describe:<ul><li> an activity that continues for a long time </li><li> an action that is repeated for a longer period of time </li></ul>These continue up to the present. You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span> when a long-continuing activity has just ended. <br> To put emphasis on the action, use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous</span>.<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">What have the other people in the cafe been doing?</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sentence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She's just been staring into space.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She is spending a long time doing this. The focus is on <span class=\\\"italic\\\">staring</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Has she been mugged? Is she in shock? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What happened before this sometime?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Everyone here has been ignoring her - like it's normal. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She's covered in mud. How could that have happened?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It hasn't been raining.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to stare into space", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look at nowhere", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She's just been staring into space.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to describe an odd event in a cafe.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be mugged", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be robbed of your personal belongings", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Has she been mugged?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be in shock", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be deeply surprised and troubled by a sudden event ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Is she is shock?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mud", "type": "name"}, {"content": "wet, soft earth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She's covered in mud.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to ignore", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to actively not notice or recognize", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Everyone here has been ignoring her - like it's normal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nosy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "overly curious", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I said I didn't mean to be nosy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to recognize someone", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to realize that someone is famous", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I recognized her immediately and felt so stupid!!!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "autograph", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person's signature", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did you get her autograph?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Outline a storyline that you can text a friend or classmate about.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make sure you have all the details 